{{Quote|Do you see the conditions I'm living in? That insipid ''senator'' put me in here! She deserves to ''die'' for leaving me to rot in this ''squalor''!|Ziro the Hutt, on Padmé Amidala|<ref name="Assassin">{{TCW|Assassin (episode)}}</ref>}}
The '''Republic Judiciary Central Detention Center''',<ref name="Deception">{{TCW|Deception}}</ref> also known as the '''Republic Correctional Facility''',<ref name="Brothers and Sisters">{{StoryCite|story=Brothers and Sisters|book=The High Republic Adventures Phase III Annual}}</ref> was a high-security [[prison]] located on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]<ref name="Deception" /> in the [[Federal District]] in the planet's northern hemisphere.<ref name="Cataclysm">''[[The High Republic: Cataclysm]]''</ref> Inside was a large panopticon of cells where high-risk [[prisoner]]s were held as well as generic cell blocks, a mess hall, a workout area, guard monitoring stations, a cremation center, and an infirmary.<ref name="Deception" /> The prison was active during the [[High Republic Era]]. After turning against the [[Path of the Open Hand]] in the [[Night of Sorrow]] and deciding to finish his prison sentence, [[Axel Greylark]]&mdash;after recovering from his injuries aboard a [[Hospital ship|medical frigate]] over Coruscant and spending another day aboard to speak with his mother [[Kyong Greylark]] and friend [[Jedi Knight]] [[Gella Nattai]]&mdash;boarded a [[shuttle]] for transfer to the Central Detention Center.<ref name="Cataclysm" /> The prison was guarded during the [[Clone Wars]]<ref name="Deception" /> by 3,200 [[Imperial shock trooper|clone shock troopers]] of the [[Coruscant Guard]] and was maintained by 64,000 staff members. A [[Warden|chief warden]] reported directly to the [[Supreme Chancellor]].<ref name="BMF 67" />

People who were held at the Central Detention Center during the Clone Wars included [[Ziro Desilijic Tiure|Ziro the Hutt]],<ref name="Hostage Crisis" /> [[Cad Bane]], [[Moralo Eval]], [[Bossk'wassak'Cradossk|Bossk]], [[Boba Fett]],<ref name="Deception" /> [[Aurra Sing]], [[Poggle the Lesser]],<ref name="Assassin" /> and [[Risha Synata]].<ref name="Intermission 2">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=13|story=Intermission, Part 2}}</ref> [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] went undercover into the prison as Jedi-killer [[Rako Hardeen]] to uncover a plot against Supreme Chancellor [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]].<ref name="Deception" />

